2 CONT # The Swedish Finn Anders Chydenius was one of the most notable politicians of 18th century Finland. He was a clergyman, Member of Parliament, economist, and one of Finland’s first exponents of economic liberalism. https://www.swe
2 CONC dishfinnhistoricalsociety.org/anders-chydenius/
2 CONT
2 CONT # Known as the Adam Smith of the North, Anders Chydenius laid out his economic prescription for mercantilist [Sweden-Finland] in The National Gain in 1765 https://www.acton.org/pub/religion-liberty/volume-16-number-3/anders-chyden
2 CONC ius
2 CONT
2 CONT # The 18th-​century writer, politician, and clergyman Anders Chydenius is one of the great founding fathers of Nordic classical liberalism. He played a crucial role in repealing restrictive economic policies, promoting religious t
2 CONC oleration, and most importantly, abolishing censorship and protecting free speech. https://www.libertarianism.org/podcasts/portraits-liberty/anders-chydenius
