1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the wife of https://www.geni.com/people/Andrew-Ross-1st-of-Balblair/6000000026922555854
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.baronage.co.uk/bphtm-03/fraser03.html “Fraser of Lovat”] 
2 CONT
2 CONT The heir: Hugh Fraser, 7th Lord Fraser of Lovat, b 1592, m 1614 Isabel (d 1636) dtr of Sir John Wemyss of Wemyss by his 2nd wife Mary dtr of James Stewart, 1st Lord Doune, and d 16 Feb 1646 having had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT >..a1. Mary Fraser, b 1617, m 1635 David Ross of Balnagowan, and d 1659
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Ane Breve Cronicle of the Earlis of Ross. Including notices of the Abbots of Fearn, and of the family of Ross of Balnagown.  by Ross, Earls of; Baillie, W. R.  Page 29-30.  [https://archive.org/details/anebrevecronicle1850ross/pag
2 CONC e/29/mode/1up Archive.Org] 
2 CONT
2 CONT >David Ross, laird of Balnagown, maried my Lord Lo- vatt's daughter, callit Marie Fraser, who bure to him seve- rall children. Bot of meall children non cairn to perfection bot David Ross, now leard of Balnagown, who maried Ladie 
2 CONC Ann Steuart, daughter to James earle of Murray. (4)
2 CONT
2 CONT > 4. David (3) was born 14th September 1644, and a brother, Alexander, on 13th September 1645. Their mother died on 29th December 1646. Deuchar MS.
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.greatclanross.org/htext6.html :
2 CONT
2 CONT >David Ross, twelfth Baron of Balnagowan, was quite young when he inherited the estates, but he was quick to suppress crime in Ross-shire. At his own expense, David raised a regiment of 800 men of Ross for the Scottish army in ord
2 CONC er to reinstate King Charles II, but they were defeated by Cromwell at the battle of Worcester in 1651 and members of the clan were either slain or taken prisoner to be sold as slaves. The considerable expense of outfitting his re
2 CONC giment with weapons and the red Ross tartan trews left David's estates in greater debt than before. He died after two years of imprisonment in the Tower of London, and he was buried at Westminster on December 29, 1653. David had m
2 CONC arried Marie, the eldest daughter of Lord Fraser of Lovat, leaving as issue: (1) David, who became the last laird of Balnagowan; (2) Alexander, who died at 20; (3) Isobell, and (4) Catherine, who married John Mackenzie, fourth of 
2 CONC Inveraul.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I1515&tree=CC cites 
2 CONT *[S6] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Ross02.
2 CONT *[S6] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Fraser02.
2 CONT *[S86] Balnagowan, J. Douglas Ross, (http://www.greatclanross.org/htext6.html), http://www.greatclanross.org/htext6.html.
2 CONT *[S6] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Fraser02: TSP (Lovat), BP1934 (Lovat). 
2 CONT * Rossiana; papers and documents relating to the history and genealogy of the ancient and noble house of Ross, of Ross-shire, Scotland, and its descent form the ancient earls of Ross, together with the descent of the ancient and h
2 CONC istoric family of Read, from Rede of Trough-end, Reade of Barton Court, Berks, and Read of Delaware. Also some account of the related families.  Author: Read, Harmon Pumpelly, 1860- [from old catalog],Reid, Francis Nevile, 1826-18
2 CONC 92.  Page 13.  [https://archive.org/details/rossianapapersdo01read/page/13/mode/1up Archive.Org] --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT When Lady Mary Catherine Fraser was born in 1617, in Beauly, Inverness-shire, Scotland, her father, Hugh Fraser 15th of Lovat, 7th Lord Fraser of Lovat, was 26 and her mother, Lady Isabel Wemyss Baroness of Wemyss, 9th Baroness of
2 CONC  Lovat, was 29. She married Laird David Ross 12th of Balnagown in 1632, in Inverness-shire, Scotland, United Kingdom. They were the parents of at least 5 sons and 3 daughters. She died on 22 December 1646, in Ardmore, Eddrachillis
2 CONC , Sutherland, Scotland, United Kingdom, at the age of 29, and was buried in Ardmore, Eddrachillis, Sutherland, Scotland, United Kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT MORE
